      "writtenOn": "2018-12-07T11:37:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as I know, the current implementation of defining a PON level service flow per direction(e.g. upstream and downstream) requires 2 flows each of which is directed to the OLT and ONT device adapters. Currently, determining which flow is going to be redirected to the ingress device or egress device is handled by looking at whether next table id  exists or not. However, with the technology profile feature coming in, this assumption is not sufficient any more due to some updates inside the service flows. What I mean in other words is, if a flow (let\u0027s say for upstream direction)  includes a table id which is smaller that TECH_PROF_ID(64), then we should say that this flow is going to be directed to the ONT adapter (ingress port), otherwise it should be directed to OLT adapter (egress port). That\u0027s why basically I added such an extra control to the corresponding if-else statement.",
      "parentUuid": "eadc20d9_2b04d5d4",
